<title>USA: Santa Fe Energy sees $2.2 mln dry hole cost.</title>
<headline>Santa Fe Energy sees $2.2 mln dry hole cost.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Santa Fe Energy Resources said it will take a $2.2 million charge as a result of its 25 percent working interest in a dry hole drilled on Garden Banks Block 370 in the Gulf of Mexico.</p>
<p>In a separate drilling program with Reading &amp; Bates Development Co., Santa Fe is drilling its Amundsen prospect in East Breaks 335 and will drill at least two additional exploratory prospects in the Flex Trend before the end of 1997.</p>
<p>((David Chance New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
</text>
